1 REM ---------------------------------------------------------------
2 REM BENCH - HOW FAST IS THIS MACHINE, IN TICKS OF THE GAME LOOP
3 REM
4 REM THERE IS NO CLOCK IN THIS BASIC, SO THE HUMAN IS THE CLOCK:
5 REM START A STOPWATCH WHEN THE STAR APPEARS AND STOP IT WHEN THE
6 REM NEXT ONE DOES. EACH TEST DOES 2000 ROUNDS.
7 REM
8 REM TEST 1 IS THE IDLE LOOP: READ A KEY AND COUNT DOWN A TIMER,
9 REM WHICH IS WHAT THE GAME DOES WHEN NOBODY PRESSES ANYTHING.
10 REM TEST 2 ADDS TWO CELLS OF PRINTING, WHICH IS ONE MOVE OF A
11 REM PIECE IN TETRIS.BAS. THE GRAVITY TABLE AT LINE 10204 COUNTS
12 REM TICKS OF TEST 1.
13 REM ---------------------------------------------------------------
20 CLS
30 PRINT "STOPWATCH READY? PRESS A KEY"
40 KB$=INKEY$
50 IF KB$="" THEN GOTO 40
60 PRINT "*"
70 GT%=2000
80 FOR I%=1 TO 2000
90 KB$=INKEY$
100 GT%=GT%-1
110 NEXT I%
120 PRINT "*"
130 FOR I%=1 TO 2000
140 KB$=INKEY$
150 GT%=GT%-1
160 LOCATE 30,10
170 PRINT "[]";
180 LOCATE 30,11
190 PRINT "  ";
200 NEXT I%
210 PRINT "*"
220 PRINT "IDLE TICKS AND DRAWING TICKS: 2000 EACH"
230 END
